IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-rules`
IMPORT `poa-seat`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- worked cases for the questions of the principal (poa-seat.l4), the date helpers
-- and the definitions in poa-rules.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- The deadline rules (ss 79, 133) are tested through their exported questions, which run the DEONTIC rules by
-- EVALTRACE inside the helper's CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the principal`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

`fin` MEANS `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)`
`pers` MEANS `a personal matter (including a legal matter about my personal or lifestyle affairs)`
`med` MEANS `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`
`both` MEANS `both personal and financial matters`
`fin only` MEANS `financial matters only`
`pers only` MEANS `personal matters only`
`for both` MEANS `for both personal and financial matters`
`for fin` MEANS `for financial matters only`
`for pers` MEANS `for personal matters only`
`ind` MEANS `an individual`
`TC` MEANS `a trustee company`
`PA` MEANS `the Public Advocate, as attorney`
`EPA` MEANS `an enduring power of attorney`
`REV` MEANS `an instrument of revocation`
`in time` MEANS `done in time`
`late` MEANS `done, but out of time`
`still open` MEANS `not done yet, and still in time`
`passed` MEANS `not done, and the time has passed`
`no limit` MEANS `no time limit under this provision`
`from making` MEANS `yes: from the making of the power (s 39(1)(a), (2))`
`not yet` MEANS `no: not yet; the time I specified has not come and I have capacity for the matter (s 39)`
`while lacking` MEANS `yes: while I do not have decision making capacity for the matter (s 39(1)(b), (3))`
`s 83 no` MEANS `no: VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order covering the matter and has not authorised my attorney (s 83)`
`s 83 yes` MEANS `yes, but only so far as VCAT has authorised, as VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order (s 83)`
`no cover` MEANS `no: my power does not cover this matter (s 22(2))`
`cease` MEANS `when I cease to have decision making capacity for the matter`
`other time` MEANS `another time, circumstance or occasion`
`executed` MEANS `yes: executed as the Act requires`
`bad witness` MEANS `no: a witness was not eligible (s 35(2) or s 48(2))`
`in force` MEANS `yes: nothing in Part 5 or Part 8 has ended it as to this attorney`
`conflict no` MEANS `no: a conflict transaction my attorney must not enter into without my or VCAT's authority (s 64(1))`
`excepted` MEANS `yes: s 64(2) takes it out of the duty`
`none` MEANS `no exception`
`joint buy` MEANS `acquiring property to be held jointly with my attorney, or a loan or guarantee for it`
`joint deal` MEANS `dealing with property my attorney and I hold jointly, or a loan or guarantee for it`
`comp yes` MEANS `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my attorney to compensate me (s 77(1))`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 2 2028) `to` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 14 3 2028

§§ `s 3 -- definitions`

#ASSERT `s 3 -- this person is my care worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- this person is my care worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- this person is my care worker` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 -- this person is my care worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
